{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, jointly set MAXLEN=64 and LR=6e-4, retaining width 64, two blocks, two heads and dropout 0.1. Most histories fit within 64 positions; shorter attention should reduce computation, while the modestly lower learning rate may stabilize optimization after removing long contexts. Preserve features, embedding tying/radius, interaction/readout and loss. Keep seeds, 200-epoch cap and 200 batches per epoch fixed; synchronize checkpoint metadata and predictor construction.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace only the Transformer feed-forward GELU activation with SiLU, retaining pre-normalization, two blocks, existing heads, 2× feed-forward width and residual paths. SiLU's smooth gating may improve contextual item interactions without adding parameters or materially increasing computation. Preserve features, embedding parameterization, history/readout, loss and optimizer. Update the predictor writer to instantiate the same activation, loading one checkpoint per category.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, change only masked-item cross-entropy temperature from 0.8 to 1.0. Softer training logits may reduce overconfident fitting and improve candidate ranking with the incumbent's normalized tied embeddings. This requires no auxiliary forward pass, avoiding the additional work of the previous timed-out pairwise objective. Preserve masked-target selection, sampling, topology, scoring/readout, optimizer and schedule; inference remains appended-mask scoring.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, reduce only the tied normalized item-embedding radius multiplier from 0.8 to 0.75, retaining width 64 and input/output tying. The regression at 0.9 motivates testing a smaller local reduction that may regularize item representations without the larger change to 0.65. Preserve features, topology, interaction/scoring, history, loss temperature and optimizer. Apply the same radius in training and the generated predictor, with one checkpoint per category."
}
